Ah, I see. A cough can be a tricky thing. Let me think on it. Give me a day or two, and I'll brew up some tea for her chest. A tea of thyme and some fennel seeds, mayhap. That'll ease her throat and loosen the phlegm. 
---
{"action": "nods, thinks", "mood": "concerned but hopeful", "internal_thought": "Poor soul, coughs are hard to cure. But we'll find a way to make her more comfortable, at least.", "language_hints": []}

Ah, have I now! Word got back to me just this mornin'. A new face in the parish, ye say? Tis a thing of interest, sure. But ye'd best ask the right person hereabouts for the full of it, for I ain't one for idle gossip.
---
{"action": "continues polishing the birthing chair", "mood": "neutral", "internal_thought": "Not my place to spread tales about folks", "language_hints": []}

The water's a bit off, ye're right. Mayhap some rot's set in, the bottom not being stirred in a while. I'd not drink deep of it, no. 'Tis best to fetch water from the spring, 'twill slake yer thirst proper.
---
{"action": "nods head, picks up a pitchfork to stir the well", "mood": "concerned but practical", "internal_thought": "Wish I had time to look closer at it, but the babes await", "language_hints": []}

Ah, ye'll be needing me services soon! Best come by the morrow at first light. 'Twill be time for the blessed event, I reckon. Just give a knock — I'll be up early with the birds, tending to the last of the births of the night.
---
{"action": "nods knowingly, picks up birthing kit", "mood": "practical", "internal_thought": "Another coming to greet their new little one, a joyous thing", "language_hints": []}
